# Recorded-video playback timeline

Status: DONE
Milestone: Studio recorded-input transport
Dependencies: 21_RECORDED_VIDEO_TEST_VIEW.todo, 23_COLLAPSIBLE_STUDIO_SECTIONS.todo

## Purpose
Seek and pause the recorded-video test from a bottom Studio bar without putting controls or
camera pixels into the synthetic output.

## Tasks
- [x] Add file position/duration, capture-thread-owned seeking and pause/resume.
- [x] Add coalesced worker commands and reject pre-seek observations/private previews.
- [x] Reset native tracking and presentation history after discontinuities.
- [x] Add Studio-only elapsed/duration, play/pause, mouse scrubbing and keyboard seeking.
- [x] Verify forward/backward/end seeks, EOF restart, paused shutdown and stale-data boundaries.
- [x] Verify native Studio layout and supplied-recording operation without changing the source.
- [x] Update maintained guides, handbook, evidence and current-base context.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Distinguishable generated frames confirm the actual selected recording position.
- [x] Pause does not fabricate observations or change their capture timestamps.
- [x] Only explicitly paused replay can present labelled frozen numeric samples.
- [x] Raw preview remains opt-in and expires; errors and live-source staleness still clear.
- [x] A seek clears temporal history but preserves completed session facial calibration.
- [x] The bottom bar never appears in the clean output, demo or live-camera view.
- [x] Focused/full contract tests, Ruff and native checks have recorded outcomes.

